course: dictionary
lesson: 911
title: Bladder: a stretchy bag
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A bladder is a stretchy bag. Inside your body, the bladder holds urine (wee) until you are ready to go to the toilet. «A puppy has a tiny bladder, so taking it outside after waking, eating and playing» tells you that a small bladder fills up quickly and needs emptying often.
explain: The same word can name other bags. A «swim bladder» is a bag of gas inside a fish, and a «gall bladder» is a small organ that stores bile. Each phrase tells you the job: the bladder is the bag that holds something.
explain: Use the context to check. «Many fish have a swim bladder, a bag of gas inside the body» gives you the clue: a bag, and gas inside it. Then ask: what does the bag do? The next words say the fish can float at any depth, so the bag helps it float.
fact: A bladder is a stretchy bag that stores liquid or air.
fact: Your bladder stores urine (wee) until you go to the toilet.
fact: A bladder can be any bag inside something, like the rubber bag inside a football.
fact: A gall bladder is a small organ that stores bile, which helps break down fat.
fact: A swim bladder is a bag of gas that helps a fish float at one depth.
exercise: «A puppy has a tiny bladder, so taking it outside after waking, eating and playing» says a puppy has a tiny bladder. What does bladder mean here? | The part of the puppy that wags its tail | A small ball used in games | *The stretchy bag inside the body that stores wee | A kind of puppy food
exercise: «Many fish have a swim bladder filled with gas that lets them float.» What does a swim bladder help a fish do? | Run very fast | *Float at one depth | Hear sounds from far away
exercise: Which everyday thing is most like a bladder? | A wooden spoon | A paper plate | *A rubber bag inside a football | A glass window
test: Which phrase names a small organ that stores bile to help break down fat? | Full bladder | Swim bladder | Weak bladder | *Gall bladder
test: In everyday life, what does «a full bladder» mean? | *You need to go to the toilet | Your body has eaten too much | A fish is floating well | A football filled with air
exam: What does a goldfish's swim bladder do? | Changes the fish's colour | *Holds gas so the fish can float at one depth | Stores bile to break down fat | Makes the fish swim faster
